🧩 2. Types of Dictionary Operations
Accessing Values

Use the key to get the value.

python
print(student["name"])   # Karthikeya
Adding / Updating Items

python
student["grade"] = "A"   # add new key-value
student["age"] = 22      # update value
Removing Items

pop(key) → removes key-value pair.

del dict[key] → deletes key.

clear() → removes all items.

Dictionary Methods

keys() → returns all keys.

values() → returns all values.

items() → returns key-value pairs.

python
print(student.keys())    # dict_keys(['name', 'age', 'grade'])
📜 3. Rules & Regulations
✅ What we should do
Use dictionaries for structured data (like storing student info).

Access values using keys.

Keep keys unique.

Use methods (keys, values, items) for iteration.

Use meaningful keys (like "name", "age") instead of random ones.

